Z||000000||Smoooooth GT||08-20-2001||12:39 AM||||When I hit the WOT switch at the TB..  The selenoid's click..  But no spray from nozzle??  What could it be??  That is a good nos filter right??  Any suggestion's??  Steve<P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_3.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Smoooooth GT||08-20-2001||07:50 AM||||I guess anyone can help me... not just Shaun...  Anybody??  Thank's  Steve||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||08-20-2001||10:19 AM||||bottle full? bottle valve open? the filter is 3 pieces.. take it apart and check it.. the brass filter and the 2 outside housing pieces.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaun41178||08-20-2001||04:07 PM||||yes is the bottle valve open?  If the solenoids are clicking then that means you have it all wired properly.  Glad to hear that since some of the wires were cut.  Glad you got that figured out.<P>Actually my filter is one piece.  It should be clean but check it anyways.  Even if it was dirty it should still flow a little bit of nitrous.  Disconnect the long nitrous line from the bottle at the solenoids.  There will be a blue connector coming out of the solenoid.  This is the filter.  Unscrew that and look through it.  You should be able to see light on the other side of it.  If you cant then it needs to be cleaned out.  What I would do to clean it out is to install the filter in the nitrous feed line backwards.  It won't screw in properly but it will go in far enough to keep it from popping out like a rocket on take off.  Install in a way so that when you open the bottle the pressure coming out of the bottle will push the dirt out of the filter.  This worked great for me.  Only need to hold the bottle open for a split second.<P>Steve call me if you need help.  I can talk you through it much faster then the forum or email can do.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds||||reg||1
